WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.901 --> 00:00:11.065
Teresa was born in 1910 in what is now the small country of Macedonia.

2
00:00:11.585 --> 00:00:14.988
When she was young, she was always happy to help out at church.

3
00:00:15.829 --> 00:00:17.951
She liked to borrow books from the priest.

4
00:00:19.732 --> 00:00:22.775
"May I read some of your books about missionaries?"

5
00:00:23.255 --> 00:00:24.737
she asked the priest one day.

6
00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:26.298
"Of course you may!

7
00:00:26.698 --> 00:00:28.260
Here they are," he said.

8
00:00:28.808 --> 00:00:34.151
She read the books over and over, and she was touched by the stories about caring for others.

9
00:00:34.691 --> 00:00:38.153
Her favorite book was about the missionaries who worked in India.

10
00:00:40.334 --> 00:00:44.156
It made her think about caring for poor people in India herself.

11
00:00:44.657 --> 00:00:50.240
When Mother Teresa was 12, she asked God if she should go to India to help people as

12
00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:50.920
a missionary.

13
00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.502
She prayed about this for six years.

14
00:00:54.062 --> 00:00:57.684
When she was 18, she asked a priest about her prayers.

15
00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:01.282
"I have talked to my mother and my sisters about this.

16
00:01:01.883 --> 00:01:03.204
I have prayed a lot too.

17
00:01:04.985 --> 00:01:08.467
But how can I be sure that God wants me to go to India?"

18
00:01:08.487 --> 00:01:12.790
"You will know through your joy, my child," was his advice.

19
00:01:13.611 --> 00:01:18.854
"I would be very happy if God let me serve him and other people," she said.

20
00:01:19.475 --> 00:01:22.016
Mother Teresa knew that her heart was leading her.

21
00:01:22.837 --> 00:01:26.880
Soon after, she went to Dublin to learn English and to be trained as a nun.

22
00:01:28.244 --> 00:01:30.405
Then Mother Teresa was sent to India.

23
00:01:31.006 --> 00:01:33.727
There she learned to speak Hindi and Bengali.

24
00:01:34.228 --> 00:01:37.049
She was saddened by the way most people lived in India.

25
00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.211
Most people were very poor.

26
00:01:39.231 --> 00:01:42.633
"Oh! Look at what little they have to eat!

27
00:01:43.233 --> 00:01:44.374
How can I help them?"

28
00:01:44.754 --> 00:01:45.334
she wondered.

29
00:01:45.974 --> 00:01:47.936
"So many people here are poor."

30
00:01:50.037 --> 00:01:55.080
While she worked very hard to help the poor, she also taught children at a high school.

31
00:01:55.716 --> 00:02:01.258
After a few years, she became the school principal, but the suffering of the poor was never far

32
00:02:01.358 --> 00:02:02.038
from her mind.

33
00:02:02.058 --> 00:02:08.960
"God, I know that being a school principal is an important job because I can help poor children

34
00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:09.520
to learn.

35
00:02:12.661 --> 00:02:15.741
But who takes care of the poor people who live on the streets?

36
00:02:16.362 --> 00:02:17.802
How can I help them too?"

37
00:02:18.262 --> 00:02:18.842
she prayed.

38
00:02:19.442 --> 00:02:24.904
On September 10, 1946, Mother Teresa felt that God had given her an answer.

39
00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:30.015
She was sure that he wanted her to serve him by helping the poorest of the poor.

40
00:02:30.575 --> 00:02:32.556
She thanked him for answering her prayer.

41
00:02:32.576 --> 00:02:36.358
"I know what I must do now.

42
00:02:36.958 --> 00:02:41.241
I must live with the poorest people, but how can I help them best?"

43
00:02:41.841 --> 00:02:43.482
She decided to become a nurse.

44
00:02:44.142 --> 00:02:49.385
One day, as she was walking on a street in the slums of Calcutta, she saw a woman

45
00:02:49.525 --> 00:02:50.385
lying in the dirt.

46
00:02:50.405 --> 00:02:53.247
"Oh! She might be hurt!"

47
00:02:53.847 --> 00:02:54.908
Mother Teresa thought.

48
00:02:55.664 --> 00:02:56.665
"Are you okay?"

49
00:02:57.105 --> 00:02:57.646
she asked.

50
00:02:57.666 --> 00:03:02.549
"Oh the woman groaned.

51
00:03:03.149 --> 00:03:05.771
Mother Teresa was shocked at the woman's condition.

52
00:03:05.791 --> 00:03:08.173
"Oh, how terrible!

53
00:03:08.653 --> 00:03:11.435
Look at all the rats and ants around this woman!

54
00:03:11.955 --> 00:03:13.576
Please, help me!

55
00:03:14.097 --> 00:03:18.119
I need to take this woman to a hospital quickly," she called out.

56
00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:19.981
But no one wanted to help her.

57
00:03:20.001 --> 00:03:21.121
"Oh no!

58
00:03:21.422 --> 00:03:24.584
She smells too bad," said one passerby.

59
00:03:26.068 --> 00:03:27.109
"Just leave her there.

60
00:03:27.329 --> 00:03:29.710
She will die soon anyway," said another.

61
00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:32.071
But Mother Teresa did not give up.

62
00:03:32.091 --> 00:03:33.972
"Do not be afraid.

63
00:03:34.473 --> 00:03:37.474
I will take you to the hospital," she told the woman.

64
00:03:38.035 --> 00:03:40.896
She carefully picked her up and helped her to the hospital.

65
00:03:41.396 --> 00:03:44.678
But even at the hospital, people were not willing to help.

66
00:03:46.519 --> 00:03:47.800
"Oh, take her away!

67
00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:49.721
She smells very bad!

68
00:03:50.521 --> 00:03:54.443
She is so dirty that she might not be good for the other patients here!"

69
00:03:54.924 --> 00:03:55.384
they said.

70
00:03:56.108 --> 00:03:57.009
"Oh please!

71
00:03:57.429 --> 00:03:58.570
You must help her!

72
00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:01.152
I will not leave until you help her!"

73
00:04:01.692 --> 00:04:03.113
Mother Teresa insisted.

74
00:04:03.633 --> 00:04:06.855
Finally a doctor and a nurse agreed to care for the woman.

75
00:04:07.396 --> 00:04:10.338
They did their best, but they could not make the woman well.

76
00:04:12.739 --> 00:04:17.783
This made Mother Teresa very sad, but she did not stop helping other poor people.

77
00:04:18.343 --> 00:04:21.826
Many people in India thought Mother Teresa was wasting her time.

78
00:04:21.846 --> 00:04:24.127
"Ha! Look at that European!"

79
00:04:24.647 --> 00:04:25.108
they said.

80
00:04:25.716 --> 00:04:27.277
"What does she think she can do?

81
00:04:27.758 --> 00:04:29.559
There are too many poor people to help.

82
00:04:30.059 --> 00:04:32.541
She's foolish if she thinks she can make a difference."

83
00:04:34.723 --> 00:04:37.004
Mother Teresa, however, never gave up.

84
00:04:37.485 --> 00:04:42.928
Because of her tireless work, the people in the slums began to realize how much she cared for

85
00:04:42.969 --> 00:04:47.712
them. She taught them how to read and write and looked after them when they were sick.

86
00:04:48.212 --> 00:04:53.056
The poorest of the poor respected her, and over time others admired her too.

87
00:04:55.292 --> 00:05:02.577
In 1950 the pope gave her permission to start her own Catholic organization called the Missionaries of Charity.

88
00:05:03.078 --> 00:05:09.842
Many joined the Missionaries of Charity, becoming nuns and priests, to help Mother Teresa look after the poor

89
00:05:09.862 --> 00:05:13.685
in India and elsewhere in the world.

90
00:05:13.805 --> 00:05:18.028
In 1979 the world recognized Mother Teresa's tireless love.

91
00:05:18.548 --> 00:05:20.730
She was awarded the Nobel Peace Prize.

92
00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:27.197
When Mother Teresa was told she had won the prize, she simply said, "I am not worthy."

93
00:05:28.037 --> 00:05:32.819
Mother Teresa kept working until her death in 1997 at the age of 87.

94
00:05:34.699 --> 00:05:37.820
She was a warmhearted, caring, and deeply spiritual person.

95
00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:41.661
Her love for the poor has inspired many to follow in her footsteps.

96
00:05:42.242 --> 00:05:47.183
Since it was founded, the Missionaries of Charity has grown, and it now helps the poorest of the

97
00:05:47.243 --> 00:05:49.684
poor in almost every country in the world.
